Source: kernel-signing
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: seine <seine@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: kernel-signing
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: fixed key for reproducible kernel module signing
 A throwaway RSA key/cert pair, installed at a well-known path, so a
 kernel built with 'extends: kernel: signing-key-package: kernel-signing'
 signs its modules with the same key on every rebuild instead of a fresh
 one Debian's own packaging generates and discards each time.
 .
 Not for production: the private key is committed in the clear.
